From: computerguy526 <355510486+computerguy526@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 16:48:27 +0000
Subject: upstream-pr-2625: nvn/archive: a run that ends during its prewarm
 writes the pipelines it compiled, so Ocarina of Time's next run takes them
 from the archive instead of compiling them again

Since #1879 the timer's flushes wait for the prewarm's end, so a period is written only when it is full (2,000) or at exit. Ocarina of Time's prewarm (31,663 lines after the first frame, on 5 workers) outlives a play session, and the graceful exit gave the archive what was left of 1.5 s (a write takes 1.8-4 s per 900 bases), or nothing when a draw was still compiling its pipeline. Every warm-up run ended with 400-500 bases not written; the next run compiled 57-167 bases again and area loads stalled over 20 s.

- nvn_mtl.m: during a prewarm that is not compacting, the timer's flush hands the period over once it is DM_PSO_ARCH_WARM_FLUSH_MS old (default 60 s, 0 = off), then 120 s, 240 s, ... up to 16 min; while captures wait the timer looks again every 10 s
- hle_lifecycle.c: the graceful exit (SIGTERM) starts the archive's write before the drain (dm_gfx_quit_begin) and gives it DM_EXIT_ARCH_MS (8 s, 3 s on iOS) beyond the 1.5 s; when graphics do not suspend in 1.5 s (a draw under way) the fallback still waits for the write within the deadline, and one claim flag lets only one of the two paths write, run the exit's continuation and end the process; a hard deadline ends the process at 1.5 s + budget + 0.5 s
- nvn_mtl.m pso4_init: a start removes a <file>.mtl4a.tmp a stopped write left (the hard deadline can end the process inside a write)
- t_pso_archive / test_pso_archive.py: in fresh processes, a timer flush in the prewarm then _exit SIGTERM in the prewarm with and without a draw holding the graphics layer, and a torn write beside a good file; the timer-flush and held-draw cases write no file without the change, and the torn write's .tmp stays
- docs/reference/rendering.md: new entry; symptom index; docs/development.md; env_switches.tsv rows

Co-authored-by: uncraftablexd <352372032+uncraftablexd@users.noreply.github.com>
(cherry picked from commit 0f1ad3d87609b899d186bb87874dd092c97a589d)
